Description: Bornona fixed-layout Bangla input method for IBus
 A Bangla input method for Linux built on IBus, implementing the Bornona
 fixed key layout (see /usr/share/doc/bornona-ibus/Bornona.txt), with a
 draggable, edge-snapping floating mode-toggle bar in the spirit of
 Avro Keyboard.
 .
 After install, the floating bar autostarts for all users and makes
 Bornona the active input engine automatically. On some desktops (those
 without ibus already configured as the input method framework) you may
 need to run "im-config -n ibus" once and log back in.
